cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: preprint
title: "Dynamic Longest Palindromic Substring via Mergeable Palindrome Summaries: A Tight Θ(log³ N) Account within the Treap Framework"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Chengde"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  We study the dynamic longest palindromic substring problem under point update,
  range reversal, range cyclic shift, insertion and deletion, with whole-string
  and interval LPS queries. Inside a Treap with mergeable palindrome summaries,
  we establish O(log^3 N) worst-case cost with high probability, expected
  O(log^2 N) on random inputs, and prove that the three logarithmic factors are
  individually necessary within the framework. The paper also records withdrawn
  claims, lower bounds for the AP count and batch LCE, verification results, and
  an analysis of the distinct-palindrome extension.
keywords:
  - dynamic strings
  - longest palindromic substring
  - Treap
  - arithmetic progressions
  - LCE
  - data structures
